sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-020: Team Lead Application Decisions — Sequence Diagram
    actor TeamLead
    participant ReactUI
    participant ExpressAPI
    participant DecisionService as Decision<br/>Service
    participant PostgreSQL

    TeamLead->>ReactUI: Open Incoming Applications
    ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: GET /api/teams/:teamId/applications
    ExpressAPI->>ExpressAPI: Verify Firebase token, MFA, active verified PART, and ownership
    alt Unauthorized or invalid team
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 400, 401, 403, or 404
        ReactUI-->>TeamLead: Show protected error and keep prior queue
    else Authorized owner
        ExpressAPI->>DecisionService: List Pending applications for owned team
        DecisionService->>PostgreSQL: Query Pending requests and permitted profile projection
        PostgreSQL-->>DecisionService: Name, handle, role, institution, skills, HTTPS portfolios, and message
        DecisionService-->>ExpressAPI: Newest-first review queue
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: Pending Review items
        ReactUI-->>TeamLead: Render loading, empty, review, or retry state
    end

    TeamLead->>ReactUI: Choose Approve or Decline
    ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: POST /api/applications/:id/approve or /decline
    ExpressAPI->>ExpressAPI: Recheck authentication, role, active/verified account, and id
    ExpressAPI->>DecisionService: Load application and verify target-team ownership
    alt Non-owner, missing, or invalid
        DecisionService-->>ExpressAPI: 400, 403, or 404 with explicit code
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: No mutation
        ReactUI-->>TeamLead: Keep application and review details
    else Approve
        DecisionService->>PostgreSQL: approve_team_application RPC
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Return prior Accepted outcome on same-decision repeat
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Otherwise serialize participant/shadow-event and team
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Lock and recheck Pending application, account, team, vacancy, and capacity
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Legacy shadow-event lifecycle and event-membership checks
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Confirm membership, fill vacancy, mark Accepted, and clear target-event LFT row
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Run shared slot/full-team cascade and persist applicant alert
        alt Stale opposite decision or competing placement
            PostgreSQL-->>DecisionService: Explicit decision or approval conflict
            DecisionService-->>ExpressAPI: 409 with existing/winning outcome
            ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: Conflict details
            ReactUI-->>TeamLead: Preserve review and request refresh
        else Approval commits or same approval repeats
            PostgreSQL-->>DecisionService: Placement, cascade, and idempotency summary
            DecisionService-->>ExpressAPI: Accepted application result
            ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 200 success
            ReactUI-->>TeamLead: Remove resolved/competing rows and show notice
        end
    else Decline
        DecisionService->>PostgreSQL: decline_team_application RPC
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Lock Pending application and recheck owner
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Mark Declined and persist applicant/owner alerts
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Return prior Declined outcome without duplicate writes on repeat
        PostgreSQL-->>DecisionService: Declined or stale-opposite conflict
        DecisionService-->>ExpressAPI: 200 idempotent outcome or 409 conflict
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: Final decision result
        ReactUI-->>TeamLead: Remove on success or preserve on conflict
    end

    Note over PostgreSQL: Approval and its cascade share one transaction, but current SQL still uses Internal Shadow Event lifecycle, participant/event membership, event-derived capacity, and event-scoped availability cleanup.
    Note over ReactUI,ExpressAPI: The review query avoids email, Firebase UID, and contact handles. Response DTOs still expose eventId and internal applicant, membership, and request identifiers.

